const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"White提出对大量候选模型反复搜索后所得到的最佳表现进行数据窥探校正。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“A Reality Check for Data Snooping” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1468-0262.00152",label:{zh:"Econometrica (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"方法将候选比较置于同一零假设下，并用重采样思路评估选择后最大表现的显著性。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “A Reality Check for Data Snooping”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1468-0262.00152",label:{zh:"Econometrica (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"输入不只是一个胜出模型的收益，还包括被比较的完整规则集合、损失函数、时间序列依赖和样本划分。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “A Reality Check for Data Snooping”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1468-0262.00152",label:{zh:"Econometrica (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"它提醒研究者：从许多规则里找到表现最好的一条，并不自动构成优于基准的可靠证据。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “A Reality Check for Data Snooping”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1468-0262.00152",label:{zh:"Econometrica (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"在研究开始时冻结候选空间，保存每次变更和失败结果，并验证重采样与时间依赖结构是否相符。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “A Reality Check for Data Snooping”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1468-0262.00152",label:{zh:"Econometrica (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (2000) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Econometrica (2000)。通过统计检验不代表经济可行、可执行或对未见未来保持同样表现。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Econometrica (2000) for “A Reality Check for Data Snooping”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/1468-0262.00152",label:{zh:"Econometrica (2000) · 来源说明",en:"Econometrica (2000) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“A Reality Check for Data Snooping”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。通过统计检验不代表经济可行、可执行或对未见未来保持同样表现。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “A Reality Check for Data Snooping”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
